#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:2
msgid "Streaming frames"
msgstr "Streaming bingkai"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:4
msgid ""
"A script that captures frames on the cam can stream each frame back to the "
"host over USB. The pattern is two calls on the :class:`openmv.Camera` "
"instance: :meth:`~openmv.Camera.streaming` to turn the stream on or off, and"
" :meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_frame` to pull the next frame out of the "
"channel."
msgstr ""
"Sebuah skrip yang menangkap bingkai pada kamera dapat melakukan streaming "
"setiap bingkai kembali ke host melalui USB. Polanya adalah dua panggilan "
"pada instance :class:`openmv.Camera`\\ : :meth:`~openmv.Camera.streaming` "
"untuk mengaktifkan atau menonaktifkan stream, dan "
":meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_frame` untuk mengambil bingkai berikutnya dari "
"channel."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:12
msgid "A minimal stream-and-display loop"
msgstr "Loop stream-dan-tampilkan minimal"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:14
msgid ""
"The cam-side script is the usual snapshot loop; what is new is that the host"
" opens streaming and reads the result back::"
msgstr ""
"Skrip di sisi kamera adalah loop snapshot biasa; yang baru adalah host "
"membuka streaming dan membaca hasilnya kembali::"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:40
msgid ""
"The cam captures frames continuously; the host pulls each one out of the "
"stream buffer as it lands. The cam overwrites the stream buffer on every new"
" snapshot, so a host that polls slower than the cam captures will silently "
"drop frames -- that is the right behaviour for viewer-style use cases."
msgstr ""
"Kamera menangkap bingkai secara terus-menerus; host mengambil setiap bingkai"
" dari buffer stream saat bingkai tersebut masuk. Kamera menimpa buffer "
"stream pada setiap snapshot baru, sehingga host yang melakukan polling lebih"
" lambat dari kecepatan penangkapan kamera akan secara diam-diam melewatkan "
"bingkai -- itulah perilaku yang tepat untuk kasus penggunaan gaya viewer."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:48
msgid "The frame dict"
msgstr "Dict bingkai"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:50
msgid ""
":meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_frame` returns either :data:`None` (no frame is "
"waiting) or a :class:`dict` with five entries:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_frame` mengembalikan :data:`None` (tidak ada "
"bingkai yang menunggu) atau sebuah :class:`dict` dengan lima entri:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:55
msgid "Key"
msgstr "Kunci"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:55
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "Arti"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:57
msgid "``width``"
msgstr "``width``"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:57
msgid "Frame width in pixels."
msgstr "Lebar bingkai dalam piksel."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:58
msgid "``height``"
msgstr "``height``"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:58
msgid "Frame height in pixels."
msgstr "Tinggi bingkai dalam piksel."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:59
msgid "``format``"
msgstr "``format``"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:59
msgid ""
"Pixel-format identifier the cam declared (an integer from the cam's "
":data:`csi` constants)."
msgstr ""
"Pengidentifikasi format piksel yang dideklarasikan kamera (bilangan bulat "
"dari konstanta :data:`csi` kamera)."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:61
msgid "``depth``"
msgstr "``depth``"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:61
msgid ""
"For compressed formats (JPEG, PNG), the size of the compressed image in "
"bytes. Unused for uncompressed formats."
msgstr ""
"Untuk format terkompresi (JPEG, PNG), ukuran citra terkompresi dalam byte. "
"Tidak digunakan untuk format tidak terkompresi."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:64
msgid "``data``"
msgstr "``data``"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:64
msgid ""
"The frame as a :class:`bytes` buffer in **RGB888**. Each pixel is three "
"bytes ``(R, G, B)``; total length is ``width * height * 3``."
msgstr ""
"Bingkai sebagai buffer :class:`bytes` dalam **RGB888**\\ . Setiap piksel "
"terdiri dari tiga byte ``(R, G, B)``\\ ; total panjangnya adalah ``width * "
"height * 3``\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:67
msgid "``raw_size``"
msgstr "``raw_size``"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:67
msgid ""
"Bytes the cam sent over USB before decode. Useful for the actual throughput "
"calculation."
msgstr ""
"Byte yang dikirim kamera melalui USB sebelum dekode. Berguna untuk "
"perhitungan throughput aktual."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:71
msgid ""
"The package converts the cam's native format (``GRAYSCALE``, ``RGB565``, "
"``JPEG``) to RGB888 before returning, so the host never has to deal with the"
" bit-packed RGB565 or JPEG-decompression path itself. Grayscale frames come "
"back with the luma value replicated into all three channels."
msgstr ""
"Paket ini mengkonversi format asli kamera (\\ ``GRAYSCALE``\\ , ``RGB565``\\"
" , ``JPEG``\\ ) ke RGB888 sebelum mengembalikannya, sehingga host tidak "
"perlu menangani sendiri jalur RGB565 bit-packed atau dekompresi JPEG. "
"Bingkai skala abu-abu dikembalikan dengan nilai luma yang direplikasi ke "
"ketiga channel."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:78
msgid ""
"The ``data`` buffer is laid out row-by-row, top to bottom; feeding it "
"straight to a display library or saving it as a raw RGB file works without "
"any further shuffling."
msgstr ""
"Buffer ``data`` disusun baris demi baris, dari atas ke bawah; meneruskannya "
"langsung ke library tampilan atau menyimpannya sebagai file RGB mentah dapat"
" dilakukan tanpa pengaturan ulang lebih lanjut."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:84
msgid "Raw streaming mode"
msgstr "Mode streaming mentah"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:86
msgid ""
"By default the cam JPEG-compresses each captured frame before placing it in "
"the stream channel and :meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_frame` decompresses on the"
" host. On cams without hardware JPEG support, the software compression is "
"the slowest step in the loop. Passing ``raw=True`` skips it::"
msgstr ""
"Secara default kamera mengompresi setiap bingkai yang ditangkap dengan JPEG "
"sebelum menempatkannya di channel stream dan "
":meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_frame` melakukan dekompresi di host. Pada kamera "
"tanpa dukungan JPEG hardware, kompresi perangkat lunak adalah langkah paling"
" lambat dalam loop. Mengoper ``raw=True`` melewatinya::"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:95
msgid ""
"The cam then sends the pixel buffer uncompressed. Uncompressed frames are "
"much larger than their JPEG equivalents, so the cam scales each captured "
"frame down to fit the stream channel before sending it; the "
"``resolution=(width, height)`` argument sets that target. The host still "
"receives RGB888 in the ``data`` field -- the package converts from whatever "
"pixel format the cam reported in ``format``."
msgstr ""
"Kamera kemudian mengirimkan buffer piksel tanpa kompresi. Bingkai tidak "
"terkompresi jauh lebih besar dari padanan JPEG-nya, sehingga kamera "
"memperkecil setiap bingkai yang ditangkap agar sesuai dengan channel stream "
"sebelum mengirimkannya; argumen ``resolution=(width, height)`` menetapkan "
"target tersebut. Host tetap menerima RGB888 di field ``data`` -- paket "
"mengkonversi dari format piksel apa pun yang dilaporkan kamera di "
"``format``\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:105
msgid "Letting events drive the loop"
msgstr "Membiarkan event menggerakkan loop"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:107
msgid ""
"A polling loop that calls :meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_frame` faster than the "
"cam produces frames spends most of its time getting :data:`None` back. When "
"the host also has other work to do (a UI to update, other channels to poll),"
" :meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_status` is the cheaper check: it returns a dict "
"mapping every registered channel name to a boolean of \"data is ready\"::"
msgstr ""
"Loop polling yang memanggil :meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_frame` lebih cepat "
"dari kecepatan produksi bingkai kamera menghabiskan sebagian besar waktunya "
"untuk mendapatkan :data:`None` kembali. Ketika host juga memiliki pekerjaan "
"lain (UI yang perlu diperbarui, channel lain yang perlu di-poll), "
":meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_status` adalah pemeriksaan yang lebih ringan: ia "
"mengembalikan dict yang memetakan setiap nama channel terdaftar ke boolean "
"\"data sudah siap\"::"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:131
msgid "This is the loop shape the CLI viewer itself uses."
msgstr "Inilah bentuk loop yang digunakan CLI viewer itu sendiri."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:134
msgid "Stopping the stream"
msgstr "Menghentikan stream"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/tools/openmv-py/streaming-frames.rst:136
msgid ""
"Call :meth:`~openmv.Camera.streaming` with ``enable=False`` to stop. The cam"
" keeps running its script but no longer fills the stream buffer; "
":meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_frame` just returns :data:`None` from that point "
"on. Calling :meth:`~openmv.Camera.stop` does the same thing implicitly by "
"halting the script."
msgstr ""
"Panggil :meth:`~openmv.Camera.streaming` dengan ``enable=False`` untuk "
"berhenti. Kamera terus menjalankan skripnya tetapi tidak lagi mengisi buffer"
" stream; :meth:`~openmv.Camera.read_frame` hanya mengembalikan :data:`None` "
"mulai dari titik itu. Memanggil :meth:`~openmv.Camera.stop` melakukan hal "
"yang sama secara implisit dengan menghentikan skrip."
